faibistes@gmail.com wrote:
> Has anyone noticed any change in nethack 4 vs vanilla, gameplay-wise?
There are indeed some changes.

> I for one, have noticed these:

> - When my character was XP 1, she found a kitten on level 3. I don't
    think that's possible in vanilla.
> - She also found a gray ooze on level 3. I'm not that sure about this one.
These are both symptoms of a change from NitroHack that I'm not sure
about, which makes the character's level have no effect on monster
generation. It's not easy to outright change back to 3.4.3 behaviour,
unfortunately, given the way that NitroHack's engine works. There's an
ongoing discussion as to how much of a difference it makes; I can tell
it would make a difference in the protection racket, though. One thing I
was considering doing already before the message was to make monsters
that were initially placed on a level depend only on dungeon level, but
monsters that generate while you're on the level depend on experience
level as well. (Levels tend to have hardly any initially placed
monsters, except for special levels.) Your complaints are helping to
convince me that a change is necessary.

Re your followup message on the subject, I'm planning to make
enemies with wands less deadly in the early game, which would solve the
problem a different way. (It does feel, however, like there is probably
something wrong with vanilla if people are /expecting/ to be able to go
deep into an area full of hostile intelligent monsters without
encountering hostile intelligent monsters. Not that that should have
too much of an influence on the eventual decision.)

The other big change that you didn't mention is that the monster AI is
improved, but this is causing some problems related to pets, and making
life complex/difficult for pacifist play. There's an interim fix in
place at the moment, but it doesn't really work (you can observe it not
working if you're ever spammed with messages about your pet missing
monsters). I want to make sure that there's a better fix in place before
the release of 4.3.

